---
import PublicContentLayout from '../layouts/PublicContentLayout.astro';
import AgentTierMatrix from '../components/AgentTierMatrix.astro';
import compatibility from '../data/compatibility.json';
import { versionedAgents } from '../lib/agent-catalog';

export const prerender = true;

const title = 'Reinstate Compatibility: Agents, Versions, and Operating Systems';
const description =
  'Check Reinstate compatibility tiers for catalog agents, Claude Code and Codex version ranges, macOS, native Windows, WSL2, path mapping, and unsupported setups.';

const label = (value: string) =>
  value
    .split('-')
    .map((part) => part.charAt(0).toUpperCase() + part.slice(1))
    .join(' ');

const ranged = versionedAgents();
---

<PublicContentLayout
  {title}
  {description}
  path="/compatibility"
  eyebrow="Compatibility"
  answer="The catalog names seventeen coding agents. Encrypted sync (T5) covers Claude Code and Codex CLI. Gemini CLI, OpenCode, Grok Build, and Kimi Code CLI are T2 handoff sources. Eleven more agents are T0: named, with a reason they are not usable. Native resume stays same-vendor."
  breadcrumbs={[
    { name: 'Home', path: '/' },
    { name: 'Compatibility', path: '/compatibility' },
  ]}
  tags={['compatibility matrix', 'Claude Code versions', 'Codex versions', 'macOS', 'Windows']}
>
  <h2 id="support-tiers">Support is a tier, not a yes-or-no flag</h2>
  <p>
    T5 is encrypted same-vendor sync. T2 is a handoff source. T0 is a named agent that
    <code>rein doctor --agents</code> can explain. A T0 row is not an integration.
    Native resume stays same-vendor. Cross-agent work is an explicit portable handoff
    into a new Claude Code or Codex session.
  </p>
  <AgentTierMatrix caption="Catalog agent support tiers T0 through T5" />
  <p>
    Machine-readable status was last reviewed on
    {' '}<time datetime={compatibility.lastReviewed}>{compatibility.lastReviewed}</time>.
    The same records are available as <a href="/compatibility.json">machine-readable JSON</a>.
    Fixture evidence is pinned to commit
    <a href={`https://github.com/HarjjotSinghh/reinstate/commit/${compatibility.fixtureCommit}`}
      ><code>{compatibility.fixtureCommit.slice(0, 12)}</code></a
    >. T0 rows have no last-tested date: the evidence is the descriptor and storage page,
    not a probe.
  </p>

  <h2 id="agent-version-matrix">Tested version ranges (T5)</h2>
  <div class="pc-table-wrap">
    <table class="pc-table">
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th scope="col">Agent</th>
          <th scope="col">Tier</th>
          <th scope="col">Tested stable range</th>
          <th scope="col">Resume mode</th>
          <th scope="col">Last tested</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        {
          ranged.map((agent) => (
            <tr>
              <td><a href={agent.integrationPath}>{agent.name}</a></td>
              <td>{agent.tier}</td>
              <td>
                <code>{agent.minimumTestedVersion}</code>–<code>{agent.maximumTestedVersion}</code>
              </td>
              <td>{agent.resumeMode}</td>
              <td>
                <time datetime={agent.lastTested}>{agent.lastTested}</time>
                <br />
                <a href={agent.source}>Test source</a>
              </td>
            </tr>
          ))
        }
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
  <p>
    These ranges are the current source compatibility evidence for T5 encrypted sync on
    macOS arm64 and deterministic synthetic fixtures. They are not a claim that every
    platform row has passed physical-device certification. Prereleases and versions
    outside each inclusive range are <code>UNTESTED</code>. The
    <a href="/compatibility/agent-version-history">agent-version change tracker</a> records
    when the inclusive ranges and fail-closed behavior changed across releases.
    No catalog agent was promoted to T3 in the v0.5.0 line; Gemini CLI stays T2.
  </p>

  <h2 id="environment-matrix">Operating-system matrix</h2>
  <div class="pc-table-wrap">
    <table class="pc-table">
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th scope="col">Environment</th>
          <th scope="col">Claude Code</th>
          <th scope="col">Codex CLI</th>
          <th scope="col">Reinstate status</th>
          <th scope="col">Evidence</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        {
          compatibility.environments.map((environment) => (
            <tr>
              <td>{environment.name}</td>
              <td>{label(environment.claudeCode)}</td>
              <td>{label(environment.codex)}</td>
              <td>{label(environment.status)}</td>
              <td>
                {
                  environment.lastTested ? (
                    <time datetime={environment.lastTested}>{environment.lastTested}</time>
                  ) : (
                    'No completed result'
                  )
                }
                <br />
                <a href={environment.source}>Evidence and gate</a>
              </td>
            </tr>
          ))
        }
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <h2 id="states">What the compatibility states mean</h2>
  <dl class="pc-facts">
    <div>
      <dt>Supported</dt>
      <dd>Exact layout and version range has release evidence; discovery, push, and pull proceed.</dd>
    </div>
    <div>
      <dt>Untested</dt>
      <dd>Recognizable but unverified; discovery is read-only and writes fail closed.</dd>
    </div>
    <div>
      <dt>Unsupported</dt>
      <dd>Known-incompatible layout, version, environment, or agent; the operation stops.</dd>
    </div>
    <div>
      <dt>Not installed</dt>
      <dd>No local installation or session root found; reported as informational.</dd>
    </div>
  </dl>
  <p>
    <code>rein setup check</code> returns compatibility exit code <code>5</code> when an installed
    adapter is <code>UNTESTED</code> or <code>UNSUPPORTED</code>. Phase 1 has no unsafe
    compatibility override. Unknown layout is exit code <code>5</code>, never a best-effort parse.
  </p>

  <h2 id="cross-platform-paths">How cross-platform path compatibility works</h2>
  <p>
    Reinstate rewrites known structural paths to portable tokens such as
    <code>${'${HOME}'}</code> and <code>${'${REPO:<id>}'}</code>. The destination device expands
    those tokens using its own configured paths. The internal mapper's work-alias primitive is not
    wired into Reinstate configuration or adapters. Free-form transcript prose and unknown fields are
    left unchanged.
  </p>
  <div class="pc-callout">
    <p>Native Windows and WSL2 are separate devices.</p>
    <p>
      Do not point both environments at one shared agent-state directory. Their path semantics and
      vendor layouts differ, so each must have its own Reinstate device identity and mappings.
    </p>
  </div>

  <h2 id="unsupported">Explicitly unsupported</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>WSL1.</li>
    <li>Treating native Windows and WSL as one Reinstate device.</li>
    <li>Automatically sharing one agent-state directory between Windows and WSL.</li>
    <li>Exporting or restoring an untested agent layout.</li>
    <li>Encrypted sync for any agent other than Claude Code and Codex CLI (T5 only).</li>
    <li>Native resume for T2 handoff sources or T0 catalog names.</li>
    <li>Silent translation between vendor-native transcripts.</li>
    <li>Syncing vendor credentials, raw secrets, MCP settings, skills, or plugins.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="verify-your-device">Verify your own device</h2>
  <p>
    Run <code>rein setup check</code> before pushing real sessions. Treat its state as authoritative
    for the installed version and local layout, and review the repository's compatibility evidence
    when a vendor ships a new version.
  </p>

  <section class="pc-related" aria-labelledby="related-heading">
    <h2 id="related-heading">Compatibility resources</h2>
    <nav aria-label="Related pages">
      <a href="/integrations">Agent integrations</a>
      <a href="/compatibility/agent-version-history">Agent-version history</a>
      <a href="/tools/path-mapping-visualizer">Path-mapping visualizer</a>
      <a href="/docs/troubleshooting">Troubleshooting</a>
      <a href="/security">Security model</a>
      <a href="/changelog">Release changes</a>
    </nav>
  </section>
</PublicContentLayout>
